  "reason": "RNA-only multiprofile with scvi_n200 is the strongest evidence so far (about 0.65 accuracy/F1), but image-only evidence is sparse and weak: resnet50 multiprofile avgpool scored only 0.328 accuracy. The key uncertainty is whether the image modality has useful signal with a stronger encoder before committing budget to multimodal fusion. config_014 tests this by changing only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while keeping the same multiprofile and avgpool setting as config_011. This cleanly isolates the effect of image representation, avoids introducing multiple untested changes at once, and helps decide whether image features are worth fusing in later experiments."
